## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical diagnostic reasoning for common cross-region latency issues, focusing on DNS routing, TLS termination, and edge pathing rather than code changes.

## Key Concepts

- DNS routing and TTL effects
- TLS handshake timing across regions
- Edge NAT/firewall behavior and LB logs
- Basic network measurement tools (dig, curl, mtr, openssl)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example: measure DNS and HTTP timings in Node.js
const https = require('https');
const start = Date.now();
https.get('https://api.example.com/ping', res => {
  res.resume();
  res.on('end', () => console.log('elapsed', Date.now() - start));
});
```

## Follow-up Questions

- What are trade-offs between low vs high DNS TTL in this setup, and how would you monitor them?
- How would you validate TLS termination consistency across regions without changing apps?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DNS propagation, basic network troubleshooting, and edge-case cache issues in a multi-site setup.

## Key Concepts
- DNS TTL propagation
- Local resolvers and caches
- Basic reachability tools: curl, traceroute, dig
- Edge firewall/NAT impact on DNS/IP traffic

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js snippet to run a dig command and print results
const { exec } = require('child_process');
exec('dig +trace api.example.com', (err, stdout, stderr) => {
  if (err) { console.error(err); return; }
  console.log(stdout);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you verify TTL propagation across multiple resolvers?
- How would you safely roll DNS changes with minimal downtime?
